codex
At depth 8, the default passes four RNG-derived bytes and four unwritten buffer bytes to the memory writer. Pre-paint equality alone cannot prove that no write occurred; a write of identical bytes, a misaddressed write, or failure to reach the arm can all preserve it.

I also found an unrelated MTE comparison worth flagging: `depth == 4` follows a calculation whose values are 8, 16, 32, and 64, making its RGBA-selection branch unreachable.
